{"title":"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Show that there exists a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> of positive integers with the following property: For\nany infinite set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of primes there exist two positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a758e08845ca74e10d1d9e3ab46113de7066c298.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/1678b6a34ce0af2c238335b0e36e29d374fbc7d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\not\\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> each of which is a product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> distinct elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17d88e2fdeef66df0e37def936f39b773567278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/0/700b5cfb013a1ae8ede70610817ae2d217b85897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> denote the number of distinct prime factors of a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\nDefine the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/8/2080af4fd2a437ded79fd696ef5de289bca77f58.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A = \\{x \\in \\mathbb{Z}^+ \\mid \\omega(x) \\text{ is an even number}\\}\\]\" width=\"299\" height=\"19\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be an arbitrary infinite set of prime numbers.\n</p><p><b>1. Construction of an element <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a758e08845ca74e10d1d9e3ab46113de7066c298.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />.</b>\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is an infinite set, we can choose two distinct prime numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da20f86205627f6c2a1b72941ad9dab456fa0c0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1, p_2 \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/8/e48311aebc760cec94aafa4833d0b3e19ba13c61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = p_1 p_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />.\nBy construction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is a product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f681bd84648c174d45eed0037702cae77ed0686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> distinct elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17d88e2fdeef66df0e37def936f39b773567278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.\nThe number of distinct prime factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8e7095406bb0edecd6e71b78d29bcd93226e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega(m) = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" />.\nSince 2 is an even number, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a758e08845ca74e10d1d9e3ab46113de7066c298.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> by the definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><b>2. Construction of an element <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/8/b6846460b2a4bf08de6073bed4dfc8eb4ff22214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\notin A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" />.</b>\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is infinite, we can also choose three distinct prime numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/a/c8a76ba74cdd703770eead02ef0b3411207c07d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q_1, q_2, q_3 \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/2/ee2ac56266b1fe82469687c90a7c93fb95268710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = q_1 q_2 q_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"13\" />.\nBy construction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/3359f43f0fd0ed3b672d389374aecd0360921a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> distinct elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17d88e2fdeef66df0e37def936f39b773567278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.\nThe number of distinct prime factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72fd451a2978dabec57eabb31fecb6d9c33d94f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega(n) = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />.\nSince 3 is an odd number, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/8/b6846460b2a4bf08de6073bed4dfc8eb4ff22214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\notin A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>We have shown that for any infinite set of primes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, there exist two positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a758e08845ca74e10d1d9e3ab46113de7066c298.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/8/b6846460b2a4bf08de6073bed4dfc8eb4ff22214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\notin A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" />, each of which is a product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17d88e2fdeef66df0e37def936f39b773567278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> distinct elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>———\nDear, above is incorrect, because 2≠3.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO\" title=\"1994 IMO\">1994 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017184714\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 237/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 866/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/20971